{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794535893967,"sessionID":"ses_e2d54b73fffeVFUa7eufkRporf","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2aca97a001No0ppCC3XrgwJU","sessionID":"ses_e2d54b73fffeVFUa7eufkRporf","messageID":"msg_1d2ac71bf0010JSOmWKA9d2z7t","type":"tool","id":"call_5682c1ebd37f4cb9ad793800","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt","offset":100,"limit":40},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt, lines 100-139\n100: | `local` | A real file or folder of the repo's own. Left alone |\n101: | `source-missing` | The checkout has no such path. Nothing is planned |\n102: \n103: ## 6. The Ordered Steps\n104: \n105: This is the checklist, and it is also what `list`, `?` and `menu` print. Each step carries its exact command, its class and one line of why.\n106: \n107: The class column is the manifest's `mutating` value for the route that owns the printed command, verbatim, so it is read from the route table and never guessed. A command with no route of its own prints `n/a`.\n108: \n109: ```text\n110: 1) /doctor:symlink link --root <dir> --runtimes <list> --mode <shape>   [class]\n111:    Why: creates the links. It shows a plan first and asks before it writes.\n112: \n113: 2) /doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>   [class]\n114:    Why: keeps the repo's own AGENTS.md and refreshes the shipped sections into it. Dropped when the instruction choice is link.\n115: \n116: 3) /doctor:mcp install   [class]\n117:    Why: builds and registers Code Mode. Run it from the Skilled checkout.\n118: \n119: 4) /doctor:git setup   [class]\n120:    Why: checks the git hooks and sk-git settings, and names the repair for each one that is off. Run it from the target repo.\n121: \n122: 5) /doctor:skill-advisor embedder   [class]\n123:    Why: sets up meaning matching for commands. It shows the cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server. Run it from the target repo.\n124: \n125: 6) /doctor:setup   [class]\n126:    Why: confirms the result. Run it from the target repo.\n127: ```\n128: \n129: Run them in this order. Step 1 takes `--link-instructions` when the instruction choice is `link`.\n130: \n131: When the workflow renders the checklist after the check, print this header above the steps:\n132: \n133: ```text\n134: DOCTOR INSTALL — [the target repo]\n135: Source: [the Skilled checkout]\n136: Runtimes: [the runtime list]   Link shape: [auto|whole|merge]   Instruction file: [embed|link]\n137: ```\n138: \n139: A printed step is handed back, never run: each writing command shows its own plan, asks its own yes and writes under its own gate. This command adds no argument to a printed command beyond the values the operator gave.\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 140]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt, lines 100-139\n100: | `local` | A real file or folder of the repo's own. Left alone |\n101: | `source-missing` | The checkout has no such path. Nothing is planned |\n102: \n103: ## 6. The Ordered Steps\n104: \n105: This is the checklist, and it is also what `list`, `?` and `menu` print. Each step carries its exact command, its class and one line of why.\n106: \n107: The class column is the manifest's `mutating` value for the route that owns the printed command, verbatim, so it is read from the route table and never guessed. A command with no route of its own prints `n/a`.\n108: \n109: ```text\n110: 1) /doctor:symlink link --root <dir> --runtimes <list> --mode <shape>   [class]\n111:    Why: creates the links. It shows a plan first and asks before it writes.\n112: \n113: 2) /doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>   [class]\n114:    Why: keeps the repo's own AGENTS.md and refreshes the shipped sections into it. Dropped when the instruction choice is link.\n115: \n116: 3) /doctor:mcp install   [class]\n117:    Why: builds and registers Code Mode. Run it from the Skilled checkout.\n118: \n119: 4) /doctor:git setup   [class]\n120:    Why: checks the git hooks and sk-git settings, and names the repair for each one that is off. Run it from the target repo.\n121: \n122: 5) /doctor:skill-advisor embedder   [class]\n123:    Why: sets up meaning matching for commands. It shows the cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server. Run it from the target repo.\n124: \n125: 6) /doctor:setup   [class]\n126:    Why: confirms the result. Run it from the target repo.\n127: ```\n128: \n129: Run them in this order. Step 1 takes `--link-instructions` when the instruction choice is `link`.\n130: \n131: When the workflow renders the checklist after the check, print this header above the steps:\n132: \n133: ```text\n134: DOCTOR INSTALL — [the target repo]\n135: Source: [the Skilled checkout]\n136: Runtimes: [the runtime list]   Link shape: [auto|whole|merge]   Instruction file: [embed|link]\n137: ```\n138: \n139: A printed step is handed back, never run: each writing command shows its own plan, asks its own yes and writes under its own gate. This command adds no argument to a printed command beyond the values the operator gave.\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 140]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt\",\"offset\":100,\"limit\":40}"},"time":{"start":1794535893370,"end":1794535893967}}}}
